<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abimael Guzmán</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1934">1934</a>–<a href="/years/2021">2021</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Chairman Gonzalo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abimael Guzmán was a Peruvian philosophy professor who founded and led the Maoist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shining-path">Shining Path</a>, known to his followers as Chairman Gonzalo. From the University of Huamanga in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayacucho">Ayacucho</a> he prepared an armed struggle, launched in May 1980, that brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> close to collapse and cost tens of thousands of lives. He was captured in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in September 1992 and died in prison in 2021, serving a life sentence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abimael-guzman.jpg" alt="Abimael Guzmán" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: altemark · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abimael_Guzm%C3%A1n_Sendero_Luminoso.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The military government handed power back in 1980, but on the eve of the elections the Maoist Shining Path, led by <b>Abimael Guzmán</b>, began an armed struggle in Ayacucho.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-peru">Republic of Peru · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>The Communist Party of the Philippines was founded on Mao’s birthday in 1968, and Peru’s Shining Path under <b>Abimael Guzmán</b> waged a prolonged people’s war.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/maoism">Maoism · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li></ul></section>
